{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01X6og4JMygajCi9suAPLJEJ","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"intervals.icu workout_doc API hr target units %lthr start end step format\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"API access to Intervals.icu\",\"url\":\"https://forum.intervals.icu/t/api-access-to-intervals-icu/609?page=7\"},{\"title\":\"HR target workouts broken on Edge 840 firmware ≥30.18 — interpreted as %HRmax instead of bpm\",\"url\":\"https://forum.intervals.icu/t/hr-target-workouts-broken-on-edge-840-firmware-30-18-interpreted-as-hrmax-instead-of-bpm/130090\"},{\"title\":\"API access to Intervals.icu\",\"url\":\"https://forum.intervals.icu/t/api-access-to-intervals-icu/609/129\"},{\"title\":\"API access to Intervals.icu\",\"url\":\"https://forum.intervals.icu/t/api-access-to-intervals-icu/609/389\"},{\"title\":\"API access to Intervals.icu\",\"url\":\"https://forum.intervals.icu/t/api-access-to-intervals-icu/609?page=20\"},{\"title\":\"# Intervals.icu Cycling Workout Syntax\",\"url\":\"https://glama.ai/mcp/servers/@gesteves/domestique/blob/20812aa55701874b27ac02c5fde692861f748452/src/resources/cycling-workout-syntax.md\"},{\"title\":\"# Intervals.icu Running Workout Syntax\",\"url\":\"https://glama.ai/mcp/servers/@gesteves/domestique/blob/213d5f7b06df7793bfdba7feb49869bae4075379/src/resources/run-workout-syntax.md\"},{\"title\":\"Feature request: Native Heart Rate Reserve (%HRR / Karvonen) heart-rate zones\",\"url\":\"https://forum.intervals.icu/t/feature-request-native-heart-rate-reserve-hrr-karvonen-heart-rate-zones/132356\"},{\"title\":\"9822 convert training prescriptions to intervalsicu workouts with claude opus ai\",\"url\":\"https://n8n.io/workflows/9822-convert-training-prescriptions-to-intervalsicu-workouts-with-claude-opus-ai/\"}]\n\nThe search didn't turn up an official spec for `workout_doc` HR targets, so this is based on forum posts and third-party docs.\n\n- **HR step shape:** A forum example for a bpm-based Z2 step uses a `target` of `\"HR\"` and a step `hr` object with `start`, `end`, and `units: \"bpm\"` (\"hr\": {\"start\": 122, \"end\": 147, \"units\": \"bpm\"}). This comes from a bug report about Edge 840 firmware, not official docs.\n- **%LTHR vs %HR:** A developer said that HR based workouts editing can only support %HR (and not absolute HR). The developer later added lthr, max_hr, threshold_pace and pace_units to the export. I found no confirmed example of a `%lthr` unit string in `workout_doc`, so verify that against the live API or the docs.\n- **Power step shape:** The power equivalent is a step with \"power\": { \"value\": 43, \"units\": \"%ftp\" }, plus a top-level `ftp` field in the export.\n- **Ranges:** Intervals.icu default range for power and pace is 2.5%. For HR it is 1.5%. The `hrRange` query parameter can change this, and use 0.0 to disable range.\n- **Download endpoints:** A developer noted that this endpoint works: /api/v1/athlete/{id}/events/{eventId}/download{ext}. A separate bug report says the public `.zwo` export strips bpm targets entirely, so check the format you export.\n- **Step text syntax:** A third-party MCP syntax guide lists targets like `75%` for FTP and `220w` for watts, but this is a text-workout format, not the `workout_doc` JSON (Percent of FTP | N% | 75%, 88%, 95-105%).\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d78efd7c-b211-45bb-ba6d-b12c4dc94d3b","uuid":"cf219bb4-469b-4020-bdc0-10a45e3f6531","timestamp":"2026-10-27T05:02:33.392Z","tool_use_result":{"query":"intervals.icu workout_doc API hr target units %lthr start end step format","results":[{"tool_use_id":"srvtoolu_01Ujo2XHFwDCzo8jkEHRiD9k","content":[{"title":"API access to Intervals.icu","url":"https://forum.intervals.icu/t/api-access-to-intervals-icu/609?page=7"},{"title":"HR target workouts broken on Edge 840 firmware ≥30.18 — interpreted as %HRmax ins