{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01HnjdkYFxmobdqNKPUvssUa","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"intervals.icu API workout_doc step \"hr\" \"units\" \"%lthr\" \"start\" \"end\" example JSON\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"API access to Intervals.icu - Page 7 - Guide - Intervals.icu Forum\",\"url\":\"https://forum.intervals.icu/t/api-access-to-intervals-icu/609?page=7\"},{\"title\":\"API access to Intervals.icu - Page 22 - Guide - Intervals.icu Forum\",\"url\":\"https://forum.intervals.icu/t/api-access-to-intervals-icu/609?page=22\"},{\"title\":\"API: Create or update workout without using description text syntax? - External Projects - Intervals.icu Forum\",\"url\":\"https://forum.intervals.icu/t/api-create-or-update-workout-without-using-description-text-syntax/124215\"},{\"title\":\"API access to Intervals.icu - Guide - Intervals.icu Forum\",\"url\":\"https://forum.intervals.icu/t/api-access-to-intervals-icu/609\"},{\"title\":\"API access to Intervals.icu - Page 20 - Guide - Intervals.icu Forum\",\"url\":\"https://forum.intervals.icu/t/api-access-to-intervals-icu/609?page=20\"},{\"title\":\"Downloading planned workouts from the API - Guide - Intervals.icu Forum\",\"url\":\"https://forum.intervals.icu/t/downloading-planned-workouts-from-the-api/93737\"},{\"title\":\"Uploading JSON , cannot get steps to be generated? - Uncategorized - Intervals.icu Forum\",\"url\":\"https://forum.intervals.icu/t/uploading-json-cannot-get-steps-to-be-generated/117959\"},{\"title\":\"Error creating a new workout plan via API due to JSON parsing - Intervals.icu Forum\",\"url\":\"https://forum.intervals.icu/t/error-creating-a-new-workout-plan-via-api-due-to-json-parsing/111518\"},{\"title\":\"Intervals Icu Api\",\"url\":\"https://openclaw.army/ar/skills/pseuss/intervals-icu-api/\"},{\"title\":\"Automate Your Training Uploads with a Python Script - Uncategorized - Intervals.icu Forum\",\"url\":\"https://forum.intervals.icu/t/automate-your-training-uploads-with-a-python-script/84863\"}]\n\nThe search didn't turn up an example of an HR step using `\"units\": \"%lthr\"`. It did turn up some related details from the Intervals.icu forum, which are mostly community posts rather than official docs.\n\n- **Step structure:** Steps in `workout_doc` use a `duration` plus a target object, and power targets take the form `\"power\": {\"value\": ..., \"units\": \"%ftp\"}`. One forum post shows a step with `start` and `end` values in the same target object, with `\"units\"` set to `%ftp` ([forum.intervals.icu, API access, page 22](https://forum.intervals.icu/t/api-access-to-intervals-icu/609?page=22)). An HR step would most likely follow the same pattern, but I didn't find a confirmed example.\n- **HR units limitation:** One developer reported that HR-based workouts could only be edited with percentage-of-HR targets, not absolute heart rate, and that LTHR or max HR values needed a separate API call ([forum, page 7](https://forum.intervals.icu/t/api-access-to-intervals-icu/609?page=7)). That post is about 4.5 years old, so it may be outdated.\n- **Resolved values:** Adding `resolve=true` to the events GET request reportedly converts steps into actual watts, bpm, or m/s, and includes the `lthr` value in `workout_doc` ([forum, page 22](https://forum.intervals.icu/t/api-access-to-intervals-icu/609?page=22)).\n- **Creating workouts via JSON:** A 2026 post shows a `PUT` to the events endpoint with a `workout_doc.steps` array, which avoids the description text syntax. The example uses `%ftp` power, not HR ([forum, API create or update](https://forum.intervals.icu/t/api-create-or-update-workout-without-using-description-text-syntax/124215)).\n\nFor an authoritative answer on `%lthr` and HR `start`/`end` fields, check the official Intervals.icu API docs or try a workout in the web app and inspect the saved JSON with browser dev tools. The forum suggests that's how the app's own payloads are visible.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d78efd7c-b211-45bb-ba6d-b12c4dc94d3b","uuid":"a2d72bde-b3c9-4f34-9c02-4b342cdb583a","timestamp":"2026-10-27T05:02:42.397Z","tool_use_result":{"query":"intervals.icu API workout_doc step \"hr\" \"units\" \"%lthr\" \"start\" \"end\" example JSON","results":[{"tool_use_id":"srvtoolu_017LQWLZk2oBcHGc68ekAqTP","content":[{"title":"API access to Intervals.icu - Page 7 - Guide - Intervals.icu Forum","url":"https://forum.intervals.icu/t/api-access-to-intervals-icu/609?page=7"},{"title":"API access to Intervals.icu - Page 22 - Guide - Intervals.icu Forum","url":"https://forum.intervals.icu/t/api-access-to-intervals-icu/609?page=22"},{"title":"API: Create or update workout without using description text syntax? - External Projects - Intervals.icu Forum","url":"https://forum.intervals.icu/t/api-create-or-update-workout-without-using-description-text-syntax/124215"},{"title":"API access to Intervals.icu - Guide - Intervals.icu Forum","url":"https://forum.intervals.icu/t/api-access-to-intervals-icu/609"},{"title":"API access to Intervals.icu - Page 20 - Guide - Intervals.icu Forum","url":"https://forum.intervals.icu/t/api-access-to-intervals-icu/609?page=20"},{"title":"Downloading planned workouts from the API - Guide - Intervals.icu Forum","url":"https://forum.intervals.icu/t/downloading-planned-workouts-from-the-api/93737"},{"title":"Uploading JSON , cannot get steps to be generated? - Uncategorized - Intervals.icu Forum","url":"https://forum.intervals.icu/t/uploading-json-cannot-get-steps-to-be-generated/117959"},{"title":"Error creating a new workout plan via API due to JSON parsing - Intervals.icu Forum","url":"https://forum.intervals.icu/t/error-creating-a-new-workout-plan-via-api-due-to-json-parsing/111518"},{"title":"Intervals Icu Api","url":"https://openclaw.army/ar/skills/pseuss/intervals-icu-api/"},{"title":"Automate Your Training Upl