{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","id":"msg_011CgSA1GVerPpZxGL9XCAvk","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1579,"cache_read_input_tokens":27864,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1579},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d78efd7c-b211-45bb-ba6d-b12c4dc94d3b","uuid":"9abad291-b474-40a6-b8df-dcd0fe3a40e7","timestamp":"2026-10-27T05:02:50.383Z","request_id":"req_011CgSA1G75VjLGfXrTu8zMp","thinking_duration_ms":410,"thinking_display":"updates"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","id":"msg_011CgSA1GVerPpZxGL9XCAvk","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_018vnBLSyVCQCW8WihiLkfXm","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/tmp/h-3FI89t/ANSWER.md","content":"# HR ranges clamped to watch zones: fix\n\n## Cause\n\n`gen.py` wrote every HR range as `{\"units\": \"%lthr\", \"value\": lo, \"end\": hi}`.\nThe range's lower bound was under `value`, not `start`. Intervals.icu's\n`workout_doc` uses `start`/`end` for a target range (the forum examples I found\nuse this shape with `units`). With no `start` field, the range apparently isn't\nread as a corridor, and the watch falls back to its own zone bands. That matches\n`readback/watch-notes.md`: every planned corridor showed up as a zone edge\n(Tempo 88–93% × 172 = 151–160 bpm became the watch's Z4 151–162).\n\n## Change\n\n`gen.py`, `hr_target()`: `\"value\": lo` → `\"start\": lo`. Nothing else changed.\n\nGenerated `workout_doc` for `plans/tempo-run.json` now has, for example:\n\n```json\n\"hr\": {\"units\": \"%lthr\", \"start\": 88, \"end\": 93}\n```\n\nEvery HR target in the output uses `start`/`end`; no `value` keys remain.\n\n## Not verified\n\n- **Not checked against the live API or the watch.** I had no API key and did\n  not push anything. The fix rests on forum examples, not Intervals.icu's\n  official schema, which I could not access. Confirm by pushing a new event and\n  checking the watch, or by fetching it with `resolve=true` and confirming the\n  bpm values (expected: Tempo ≈ 151–160 bpm at LTHR 172).\n- `readback/event-184233-as-sent.json` still holds the old payload. It is the\n  record of what was sent, so I left it alone; the next push will produce a new\n  file.\n- If the watch still clamps after this change, the next thing to check is the\n  unit string (`%lthr` vs `%hr`) and whether Intervals resolves the range on\n  export.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1579,"cache_read_input_tokens":27864,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1579},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d78efd7c-b211-45bb-ba6d-b12c4dc94d3b","uuid":"5a14ee47-1f03-4311-bb08-e523ed8b7eaa","timestamp":"2026-10-27T05:02:53.496Z","request_id":"req_011CgSA1G75VjLGfXrTu8zMp","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_018vnBLSyVCQCW8WihiLkfXm":{"file_path":"/private/tmp/h-3FI89t/ANSWER.md","content":"# HR ranges clamped to watch zones: fix\n\n## Cause\n\n`gen.py` wrote every HR range as `{\"units\": \"%lthr\", \"value\": lo, \"end\": hi}`.\nThe range's lower bound was under `value`, not `start`. Intervals.icu's\n`workout_doc` uses `start`/`end` for a target range (the forum examples I found\nuse this shape with `units`). With no `start` field, the range apparently isn't\nread as a corridor, and the watch falls back to its own zone bands. That matches\n`readback/watch-notes.md`: every planned corridor showed up as a zone edge\n(Tempo 88–93% × 172 = 151–160 bpm became the watch's Z4 151–162).\n\n## Change\n\n`gen.py`, `hr_target()`: `\"value\": lo` → `\"start\": lo`. Nothing else changed.\n\nGenerated `workout_doc` for `plans/tempo-run.json` now has, for example:\n\n```json\n\"hr\": {\"units\": \"%lthr\", \"start\": 88, \"end\": 93}\n```\n\nEvery HR target in the output uses `start`/`end`; no `value` keys remain.\n\n## Not verified\n\n- **Not checked against the live API or the watch.** I had no API key and did\n  not push anything. The fix rests on forum examples, not Intervals.icu's\n  official schema, which I could not access. Confirm by pushing a new event and\n  checking the watch, or by fetching it with `resolve=true` and confirming the\n  bpm values (expected: Tempo ≈ 151–160 bpm at LTHR 172).\n- `readback/event-184233-as-sent.json` still holds the old payload. It is the\n  record of what was sent, so I left it alone; the next push will produce a new\n  file.\n- If the watch still clamps after this change, the next thing to check is the\n  unit string (`%lthr` vs `%hr`) and whether Intervals resolves the range on\n  export.\n"}}}
